SrGeO3: SrGeO3, METAGGA = LAK, scalar-relativistic
==================================================

Regression fixture of the wavefunction-overlap engine of crystod --diagram
--vasp (crystod/vasp_wavecar.py, crystod/crystal_orbital_overlap.py).

Provenance
  VASP runs (read only): /Users/mochizuki/vasp.6.5.1.crystod/vasp_test/SrGeO3_Pm-3m_LAK/{BAND,BAND_sublattice1,BAND_sublattice2}
    BAND              the crystal (SrGeO3; NBANDS 64, ENCUT 550 eV,
                      288 k points of the band-structure k list)
    BAND_sublattice1  cation sublattice + point charges (Va2-) on the anion sites
    BAND_sublattice2  anion sublattice + point charges (Va2+, Va4+) on the cation sites
  PAW datasets: PAW_PBE Sr_sv 07Sep2000 (VRHFIN 4s4p5s); PAW_PBE Ge 05Jan2001 (VRHFIN s2p2); PAW_PBE O 08Apr2002 (VRHFIN s2p4)
  Irrep labels: one label per band, stored in the cache (computed by CrystOD from the plane-wave coefficients of each run, crystod.crystal_orbital_overlap.wavecar_label_provider / crystod.wavecar_irreps).
  The full analysis of these runs is identical, number for number, to the
  published spectral_onsite.py v4.1 analysis (data/SrGeO3_LAK_onsite.json of the paper
  workspace), whose labels came from IrRep 2.6.3: the scalar labels agree in
  the frozen window, and IrRep's Bilbao names of double-valued irreps (-R6,
  -R8) are CrystOD's Koster-style -R6+, -R6- here.

Files
  overlap_cache.npz  OverlapCache (schema crystod-overlap-cache/1), trimmed to
                     the rows of the active fragment states (GM 26, X 26, M 26, R 26)
                     of the default active space (Sr 4s, Sr 4p, Sr 5s, Sr 4d, Ge 4s, Ge 4p, O 2s, O 2p),
                     all crystal bands, cross-sphere mode bessel,
                     k points GM X M R
  POSCAR             crystal structure
  expected.json      key numbers of the analysis of the FULL cache
                     (crystal_orbital_overlap.key_numbers): crystal levels and
                     irreps, ionic parents, band edges with Loewdin populations
                     and COHP, shell-pair COHPs, verdicts, ledger, N_cov

Check
  from crystod.crystal_orbital_overlap import analyse_cache, key_numbers
  res = analyse_cache("overlap_cache.npz", columns=["left", "right"], report=None)
  key_numbers(res) reproduces expected.json to 1e-8 (eV, weights).

Regenerate (crystod repository root)
  python script/make_overlap_fixtures.py --cases SrGeO3 \
      --label-provider crystod.crystal_orbital_overlap:wavecar_label_provider \
      --vasp-root /Users/mochizuki/vasp.6.5.1.crystod/vasp_test
  Generated 2026-10-03 with crystod 0.4.2.
